{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\nimport sys\nimport math\nimport itertools\n\noriginal_stdout = sys.stdout\nuse_file_io = False\n\nif use_file_io:\n    fin = open('input.txt', 'r')\n    fout = open('output.txt', 'w')\n    sys.stdout = fout\n    def read_line():\n        return fin.readline().strip()\nelse:\n    fin = sys.stdin\n    fout = sys.stdout\n    def read_line():\n        return fin.buffer.readline().strip()\n\ndef read_int_list():\n    return list(map(int, read_line().split()))\n\ndef read_int():\n    return int(read_line())\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp):\n    result = 1\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n    return result\n\ndef factorial(n):\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        result = (result * i) % MOD\n    return result\n\ndef solve():\n    n = read_int()\n    a = read_int_list()\n    b = read_int_list()\n    a1, a2, a3 = a\n    b1, b2, b3 = b\n    \n    max_possible = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n    \n    best_match = 0\n    for perm in itertools.permutations([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]):\n        ta1, ta2, ta3 = a1, a2, a3\n        tb1, tb2, tb3 = b1, b2, b3\n        current_match = 0\n        \n        for p in perm:\n            if p == 1:\n                t = min(ta1, tb1)\n                ta1 -= t\n                tb1 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 2:\n                t = min(ta1, tb3)\n                ta1 -= t\n                tb3 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 3:\n                t = min(ta2, tb2)\n                ta2 -= t\n                tb2 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 4:\n                t = min(ta2, tb1)\n                ta2 -= t\n                tb1 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 5:\n                t = min(ta3, tb3)\n                ta3 -= t\n                tb3 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 6:\n                t = min(ta3, tb2)\n                ta3 -= t\n                tb2 -= t\n                current_match += t\n        \n        best_match = max(best_match, current_match)\n    \n    print(n - best_match, mx := max_possible)\n\ndef main():\n    try:\n        t = 1\n        for _ in range(t):\n            solve()\n    finally:\n        fin.close()\n        fout.close()\n        sys.stdout = original_stdout\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static BufferedReader br;\n    private static PrintWriter out;\n    private static boolean useFileIO = false;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try {\n            if (useFileIO) {\n                br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(\"input.txt\"));\n                out = new PrintWriter(new FileWriter(\"output.txt\"));\n            } else {\n                br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n                out = new PrintWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out));\n            }\n            \n            int t = 1;\n            for (int i = 0; i < t; i++) {\n                solve();\n            }\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        } finally {\n            try {\n                br.close();\n                out.close();\n            } catch (Exception e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static String readLine() throws IOException {\n        return br.readLine().trim();\n    }\n\n    private static int readInt() throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(readLine());\n    }\n\n    private static int[] readIntList() throws IOException {\n        String[] parts = readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        int[] arr = new int[parts.length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {\n            arr[i] = Integer.parseInt(parts[i]);\n        }\n        return arr;\n    }\n\n    private static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int n = readInt();\n        int[] a = readIntList();\n        int[] b = readIntList();\n        int a1 = a[0], a2 = a[1], a3 = a[2];\n        int b1 = b[0], b2 = b[1], b3 = b[2];\n        \n        int max_possible = Math.min(a1, b2) + Math.min(a2, b3) + Math.min(a3, b1);\n        \n        int best_match = 0;\n        int[] perm = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};\n        \n        // Generate all permutations using Heap's algorithm\n        permute(perm, 0, perm.length - 1, a1, a2, a3, b1, b2, b3);\n        \n        // We need to calculate best_match during permutation generation\n        // Since Java doesn't have itertools.permutations, we'll use a different approach\n        // Let's manually compute all 720 permutations\n        best_match = calculateBestMatch(a1, a2, a3, b1, b2, b3);\n        \n        out.println((n - best_match) + \" \" + max_possible);\n    }\n    \n    private static int calculateBestMatch(int a1, int a2, int a3, int b1, int b2, int b3) {\n        int best_match = 0;\n        int[] perm = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};\n        \n        // Generate all permutations using Heap's algorithm\n        List<int[]> allPerms = new ArrayList<>();\n        permuteToList(perm, 0, perm.length - 1, allPerms);\n        \n        for (int[] p : allPerms) {\n            int ta1 = a1, ta2 = a2, ta3 = a3;\n            int tb1 = b1, tb2 = b2, tb3 = b3;\n            int current_match = 0;\n            \n            for (int val : p) {\n                if (val == 1) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta1, tb1);\n                    ta1 -= t;\n                    tb1 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                } else if (val == 2) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta1, tb3);\n                    ta1 -= t;\n                    tb3 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                } else if (val == 3) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta2, tb2);\n                    ta2 -= t;\n                    tb2 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                } else if (val == 4) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta2, tb1);\n                    ta2 -= t;\n                    tb1 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                } else if (val == 5) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta3, tb3);\n                    ta3 -= t;\n                    tb3 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                } else if (val == 6) {\n                    int t = Math.min(ta3, tb2);\n                    ta3 -= t;\n                    tb2 -= t;\n                    current_match += t;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            best_match = Math.max(best_match, current_match);\n        }\n        \n        return best_match;\n    }\n    \n    private static void permuteToList(int[] arr, int start, int end, List<int[]> result) {\n        if (start == end) {\n            result.add(arr.clone());\n        } else {\n            for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {\n                swap(arr, start, i);\n                permuteToList(arr, start + 1, end, result);\n                swap(arr, start, i);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {\n        int temp = arr[i];\n        arr[i] = arr[j];\n        arr[j] = temp;\n    }\n\n    private static void permute(int[] arr, int l, int r) {\n        if (l == r) {\n            // Process permutation\n        } else {\n            for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {\n                swap(arr, l, i);\n                permute(arr, l + 1, r);\n                swap(arr, l, i);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012420836719684303, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0002975021197926253, -1.537788011773955e-05, -0.1797524243593216, -0.002904009073972702, -4.887569048150908e-06, -8.34461570775602e-06, -9.381330892210826e-05, -0.0013974672183394432, -6.675497570540756e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.936446541454643e-05, -0.47415220737457275, -0.0010336062405258417, -0.7586493492126465, -0.006776565685868263, -0.0495271272957325, -0.950835645198822, -0.0009133219718933105, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -7.390948667307384e-06, -0.011691267602145672, -0.38846829533576965, -0.011048568412661552, -0.009757679887115955, -0.0002366024418734014, -0.0001445904199499637, -0.6502447128295898, -0.07311803847551346, -0.0004012971476186067, -0.01605382189154625, -0.0011403016978874803, -0.0003844952443614602, -0.28115272521972656, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.5788941979408264, -2.622600959512056e-06, -6.8662193370983e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.539125671319198e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.6931884288787842, -5.00